# OTD3.1 — THE SELF-MAKE TOUR: every new library in one scene.
# Written by hand, checked by the synthesizer's own compiler.
#
# Try the synthesizer that writes scenes like this one from a sentence:
#   otd --make "two balls racing to the ground, lead and pine"
# And the trainer that teaches OTD-Burn its own physics:
#   otd --train
scene "The self-make tour — six materials, one dataset"

# six spheres, six materials: a whole statistics lesson in one line each
leadBall   = sphere(r: 3cm) at (-25cm, 80cm, 0) material: lead
pineBall   = sphere(r: 3cm) at (-15cm, 80cm, 0) material: pine
steelBall  = sphere(r: 3cm) at (-5cm, 80cm, 0) material: steel
goldBall   = sphere(r: 3cm) at (5cm, 80cm, 0) material: gold
corkBall   = sphere(r: 3cm) at (15cm, 80cm, 0) material: pine color: tan
mercuryBall = sphere(r: 3cm) at (25cm, 80cm, 0) material: mercury

# the Galileo race: no mass in v = sqrt(2gh)
simulate: drop
# the scene reads itself: mean, sigma, correlation, the CLT live
simulate: stats
# the highest ball becomes a satellite: Kepler and vis-viva take over
simulate: orbit
# and a neural net learns the law they all obey
simulate: learn

ask "which lands first?"
